</script>

# Sheet

A panel docked to one edge of the viewport over a blurred backdrop. Built on the native `dialog` element with `showModal`, so it renders in the top layer above every ancestor. Clicking the backdrop, pressing Escape, or using the corner close button closes it, and the panel slides out as the backdrop fades.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Sheet, SheetTrigger, SheetContent, SheetHeader, SheetTitle, SheetDescription } from "#lib/components/ui/sheet/index.js";
</script>

<Sheet>
	<SheetTrigger>Open</SheetTrigger>
	<SheetContent>
		<SheetHeader>
			<SheetTitle>Are you absolutely sure?</SheetTitle>
			<SheetDescription>This action cannot be undone.</SheetDescription>
		</SheetHeader>
	</SheetContent>
</Sheet>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/sheet.json
```

## Anatomy

`Sheet` holds the open state and renders the modal `dialog` element and its panel while open. `SheetTrigger` opens it and renders a `Button` with its children as the label. `SheetContent` registers its children with `Sheet`, which renders them inside the panel.

Inside the content, `SheetHeader` groups a `SheetTitle` and a `SheetDescription`. The title labels the sheet and the description describes it for assistive technology. `SheetFooter` sits at the end of the panel for actions, and `SheetClose` closes the sheet.

## Trigger

To open the sheet from any other element, pass a `trigger` snippet to `SheetTrigger`. It receives `props` with an `onclick` that opens the sheet. Spread them onto the element, such as a link styled button or an icon.

<Demo section="trigger" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Sheet>
	<SheetTrigger>
		{#snippet trigger({ props })}
			<button type="button" {...props}>Open with a custom trigger</button>
		{/snippet}
	</SheetTrigger>
	<SheetContent>
		<SheetHeader>
			<SheetTitle>Custom trigger</SheetTitle>
			<SheetDescription>The trigger snippet receives the props that open the sheet.</SheetDescription>
		</SheetHeader>
	</SheetContent>
</Sheet>
```

## Close

`SheetClose` renders an outline `Button` that closes the sheet. It takes the same `trigger` snippet as `SheetTrigger`, so any element can close the sheet. Set `closeButton={false}` on `Sheet` to hide the corner close button.

<Demo section="close" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Sheet, SheetTrigger, SheetContent, SheetHeader, SheetTitle, SheetDescription, SheetFooter, SheetClose } from "#lib/components/ui/sheet/index.js";
	import { Button } from "#lib/components/ui/button/index.js";
</script>

<Sheet>
	<SheetTrigger>Edit profile</SheetTrigger>
	<SheetContent>
		<SheetHeader>
			<SheetTitle>Edit profile</SheetTitle>
			<SheetDescription>Make changes to your profile here. Click save when you are done.</SheetDescription>
		</SheetHeader>
		<SheetFooter>
			<SheetClose>
				{#snippet trigger({ props })}
					<Button {...props}>Save changes</Button>
				{/snippet}
			</SheetClose>
			<SheetClose>Cancel</SheetClose>
		</SheetFooter>
	</SheetContent>
</Sheet>
```

## Controlled

Use `bind:open` to open or close the sheet from your own code. The binding updates in both directions, so closing the sheet from the backdrop, Escape, or a close button sets the variable back to `false`. A trigger is optional.

<Demo section="controlled" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Sheet, SheetContent, SheetHeader, SheetTitle, SheetFooter } from "#lib/components/ui/sheet/index.js";
	import { Button } from "#lib/components/ui/button/index.js";

	let isOpen = $state(false);
</script>

<Button variant="outline" onclick={() => (isOpen = true)}>Open from outside</Button>

<Sheet bind:open={isOpen}>
	<SheetContent>
		<SheetHeader>
			<SheetTitle>Controlled</SheetTitle>
		</SheetHeader>
		<SheetFooter>
			<Button onclick={() => (isOpen = false)}>Done</Button>
		</SheetFooter>
	</SheetContent>
</Sheet>
```

## Side

Set `side` on `Sheet` to `top`, `right`, `bottom`, or `left` to choose the edge the panel slides in from. It defaults to `right`. Side panels fill the height up to `24rem` wide at the default size, and top and bottom panels fill the width and size to their content.

<Demo section="side" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Sheet side="left">
	<SheetTrigger>Open</SheetTrigger>
	<SheetContent>Left panel</SheetContent>
</Sheet>
```

## Variant

Set `variant` on `Sheet` to `default`, `secondary`, or `outline` to change the panel.

<Demo section="variant" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Sheet variant="secondary">
	<SheetTrigger>Open</SheetTrigger>
	<SheetContent>Secondary panel</SheetContent>
</Sheet>
```

## Size

Set `size` on `Sheet` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg` to change the panel's padding and gap, and the width of side panels from `16rem` to `32rem`. It defaults to `md`, and `xs` also shrinks the text. Unlike other sized components, the panel stays square until `rounded` is set.

<Demo section="size" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Sheet size="lg">
	<SheetTrigger>Open</SheetTrigger>
	<SheetContent>Wider and roomier.</SheetContent>
</Sheet>
```

## Rounded

The panel is square by default. Set `rounded` on `Sheet` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to round the two corners facing the page, such as the top corners of a bottom sheet. `pill` is a true pill and can clip tall content, so use `3xl` or `4xl` for round corners that stay safe.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Sheet side="bottom" rounded="lg">
	<SheetTrigger>Open</SheetTrigger>
	<SheetContent>Rounded lg</SheetContent>
</Sheet>
```

## Overrides

The default `SheetTrigger` and `SheetClose` buttons take `variant`, `size`, `rounded`, and `class`, so you can restyle them without a `trigger` snippet.

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<SheetTrigger variant="outline" size="sm">Open</SheetTrigger>
<SheetClose variant="ghost" rounded="pill">Cancel</SheetClose>
```

## API

`Sheet` extends the native `dialog` attributes, and extra attributes pass through to the dialog. `SheetHeader`, `SheetTitle`, `SheetDescription`, and `SheetFooter` extend the `header`, `h2`, `p`, and `footer` attributes.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface TriggerProps {
	/** Label for the default trigger button */
	children?: Snippet;
	/** Custom trigger; spread `props` onto the element that opens the sheet */
	trigger?: Snippet<[{ props: { onclick: () => void } }]>;
	/** Style of the default trigger button; defaults to `default` */
	variant?: ButtonProps["variant"];
	/** Size of the default trigger button, including the square `icon-*` sizes; defaults to `md` */
	size?: ButtonProps["size"];
	/** Corner radius of the default trigger button; follows its size when omitted */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}

interface CloseProps {
	/** Label for the default close button */
	children?: Snippet;
	/** Custom close trigger; spread `props` onto the element that closes the sheet */
	trigger?: Snippet<[{ props: { onclick: () => void } }]>;
	/** Style of the default close button; defaults to `outline` */
	variant?: ButtonProps["variant"];
	/** Size of the default close button, including the square `icon-*` sizes; defaults to `md` */
	size?: ButtonProps["size"];
	/** Corner radius of the default close button; follows its size when omitted */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}

interface ContentProps {
	/** Content rendered inside the sheet panel */
	children: Snippet;
}

interface Props extends CompProps<"dialog"> {
	/** Whether the sheet is shown; supports `bind:open` */
	open?: boolean;
	/** Edge of the viewport the panel slides in from; defaults to `right` */
	side?: "top" | "right" | "bottom" | "left";
	/** Visual style of the panel */
	variant?: "default" | "secondary" | "outline";
	/** Panel padding, gap, and side panel width on the shared scale; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Radius of the panel's two inner corners; square when omitted. `pill` is a true pill that can clip the content, so use `3xl` or `4xl` to stay round */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
	/** Whether to show the close button in the panel corner; defaults to `true` */
	closeButton?: boolean;
	/** The `SheetTrigger` and `SheetContent` parts */
	children: Snippet;
}
```
